<IndustryPage {...pageData}>
<p>UK manufacturing is embracing Industry 4.0, and bespoke software is at the heart of it. From MES integration that connects your shop floor to your boardroom, to custom production scheduling that replaces brittle spreadsheets, the right software transforms how manufacturers operate. Yet many UK manufacturers still rely on a patchwork of legacy ERP modules, disconnected spreadsheets, and paper-based QA records that make it impossible to see what's happening on the line in real time.</p>
<p>Off-the-shelf manufacturing software compounds the problem. Generic MES packages force you to adapt your processes to their workflow - renaming your work centres, reorganising your bill of materials, and changing how operators log downtime. They rarely integrate cleanly with older machinery or niche quality standards, and per-seat licensing punishes you for adding shop-floor users. We've seen factories where operators maintain shadow spreadsheets because the official system can't capture the nuances of a specific production line.</p>
<p>We build custom software for UK manufacturers that improves efficiency, reduces costs, and enhances quality. We understand manufacturing environments - from the production line to the supply chain - and we build systems that integrate with your existing ERP, MES, and accounting platforms. Bespoke software fits your exact workflows, terminology, and reporting needs, connecting machines, sensors, and people in a single source of truth.</p>
<p>Manufacturing compliance adds another layer of complexity. Whether you're working to ISO 9001, AS9100, or sector-specific standards like BRCGS for food production, bespoke software can automate batch traceability, manage digital sign-offs, and generate audit-ready reports on demand - eliminating the scramble when an inspector arrives unannounced.</p>
<p>A UK precision engineering firm approached us after their off-the-shelf scheduling system repeatedly double-booked critical CNC machines. We built a bespoke scheduling tool that accounted for machine capabilities, tooling availability, and operator skill levels - reducing machine idle time by 23% within three months and cutting late deliveries by nearly half. The system integrated with their existing Sage ERP, so no data entry was duplicated.</p>
<p>Manufacturing is a sector where bespoke software delivers clear ROI. The data is already being generated by machines, sensors, and ERP systems. The opportunity is building software that turns that data into actionable workflows, automated processes, and real-time visibility across your operation.</p>

